### `Military.razor.css` (Updated with Fixed/Scrolling Logic)

This CSS implements the fixed header and ensures the main content area occupies the remaining vertical space and is scrollable.

```css
/* Custom styles for the Military Applications page. */

/* 1. Define the Fixed Header and Calculate Space */
:root {
    /* Estimated height of the hero section. Adjust this if the Blazor/Bootstrap rendering changes the height. */
    --header-height: 250px;
}

.fixed-header {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 1030; /* Ensure it's above other content */
    height: var(--header-height);
    margin-bottom: 0 !important; /* Override potential Bootstrap margin */
}

/* 2. Define the Scrolling Content Container */
.scrollable-content-wrapper {
    /* Offset from the top by the header's height */
    padding-top: var(--header-height);
    /* Make it fill the rest of the viewport height (100vh - header height) */
    height: 100vh;
    overflow-y: auto; /* Enable vertical scrolling */
    overflow-x: hidden;
}

/* 3. Style for the Hero Image Placeholder on the Cards */
.card-img-placeholder {
    height: 180px; /* Defined height for visual impact */
    background-color: #343a40; /* Dark background for a serious look */
    color: #ffc107; /* Warning color for the icon */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 3.5rem; /* Large icon size */
    border-bottom: 3px solid #ffc107; /* Separator line */
}

/* Existing styles for card hover */
.card-body:hover {
    transition: transform 0.3s ease-in-out;
    transform: translateY(-5px); /* Lift the card slightly on hover */
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2); /* Stronger shadow on hover */
}